.TH QUOTA_CHECK 1 "August 2026" "bodhi" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quota_check \- report /beevol storage usage against your hard quota
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quota_check
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B quota_check
.RB [ \-\-full | \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-u
.IR USER ]
.br
.B quota_check \-\-all
.RB [ \-\-email ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quota_check
reports how much space a user is occupying on
.IR /beevol ,
and how that compares with the hard quota the administrators have set.
.PP
Usage is not held in one place. Each of the nine storage servers behind
.I /beevol
runs a small quota daemon that answers
.BI "QUOTA " uid
on TCP port 9878 with
.BI "OK " kilobytes
for its own share.
.B quota_check
asks all of them at once and adds the answers up, so one slow or
unreachable server costs a line of output rather than the whole report.
.PP
The daemons do not know what anyone's limit is. That comes from a
pipe-delimited file the administrators maintain \(em see
.B QUOTA FILE
below. Without it, usage still reports and the
.B Hard Quota
and
.B % Used
columns read
.BR \- .
.PP
With no options,
.B quota_check
prints a single summary line for the current user. Ask for
.B \-\-full
to see which server holds what.
.PP
This is a shell rewrite of the earlier Python
.BR quota_client.py .
The one deliberate change in behaviour is that the summary is now the
default: the old version printed the whole per-server breakdown unless
you remembered
.BR \-b .
That option is still accepted and now does nothing, because the
over-quota notification mail has been telling people to run
.B quota_check \-b
for years.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-u\fR,\ \fB\-\-user\  USER
Report on
.I USER
instead of the current user. Accepts a numeric uid as well as a name.
The account must resolve through
.BR getent (1)
on the host you run this from.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-full
Add the per-server breakdown, the number of servers that answered, and
what the ones that did not had to say.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit one JSON object per user \(em a bare object for a single user, an
array under
.BR \-\-all .
Sizes appear twice, as raw
.B _kb
integers and as the formatted strings the tables print.
.B percent
is
.B null
when there is no quota to compare against.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Report on every user named in the quota file rather than just one. Users
in the file with no account on this host are skipped with a warning.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-brief
Accepted and ignored; this is the default. See
.B DESCRIPTION
above.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help message.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ADMIN OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-email
Mail every user over 100% of their quota, using the address in the third
field of the quota file. Requires
.BR \-\-all .
Users over quota with no address in the file are reported on stderr and
skipped.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
With
.BR \-\-email ,
list who would be mailed without sending anything. Always run this first.
.TP
.BI \-H\fR,\ \fB\-\-hosts\  LIST
Storage servers to query, comma- or space-separated. Repeating the option
appends, so the first
.B \-H
replaces the built-in list and later ones extend it.
.TP
.BI \-p\fR,\ \fB\-\-port\  PORT
Quota daemon port. Default 9878.
.TP
.BI \-q\fR,\ \fB\-\-quota\-file\  PATH
Read hard quotas from
.I PATH
instead of searching the default locations.
.TP
.BI \-t\fR,\ \fB\-\-timeout\  SECONDS
How long to wait on any one storage server, and on the mail server.
Default 10.
.TP
.BI \-\-smtp\-server\  HOST\fR[:\fIPORT\fR]
Mail relay for
.BR \-\-email .
Default
.BR mail.ucdenver.pvt .
.TP
.BI \-\-smtp\-from\  ADDRESS
Envelope and header sender. Default
.BR noreply@cuanschutz.edu .
.TP
.BI \-\-smtp\-cc\  ADDRESS
Copy every notification here. Defaults to the storage administrator.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-smtp\-cc
Send notifications to the user only.
.SH QUOTA FILE
One user per line, pipe-delimited, with the notification address optional:
.PP
.RS
.nf
jdoe|21.48TiB|jdoe@example.com
.fi
.RE
.PP
Whitespace around the fields is padding rather than data. Blank lines and
lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored, as is any line without at least a username and a size. Sizes
accept the
.BR xfs_quota (8)
suffixes
.RB ( K ", " M ", " G ", " T ", " P )
and their IEC spellings
.RB ( KiB ", " MiB ", " GiB ", " TiB ", " PiB ),
in either case.
.PP
The file is searched for in this order, first readable copy winning:
.TP
.I /etc/quota_current.txt
The administrators' copy. Head node only.
.TP
.I /cluster/share/quota_current.txt
An NFS mount every node has, which is what makes
.B % Used
work on a compute node. Publish it with
.B make publish\-quota\-file
from the same job that regenerates
.IR /etc/quota_current.txt ,
or the compute nodes will report against a stale limit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Each of these supplies a default that the matching option overrides.
.TP
.B QUOTA_CHECK_USER
User to report on when
.B \-\-user
is not given, ahead of
.BR $USER .
.TP
.B QUOTA_CHECK_PORT
Quota daemon port.
.TP
.B QUOTA_CHECK_TIMEOUT
Per-server timeout, in seconds.
.TP
.BR QUOTA_CHECK_SMTP_SERVER ", " QUOTA_CHECK_SMTP_FROM ", " QUOTA_CHECK_SMTP_CC
Mail relay, sender, and copy address for
.BR \-\-email .
.TP
.B QUOTA_CHECK_ADMIN
Address the notification mail tells users to contact about a quota
increase.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was produced.
.TP
.B 1
No storage server answered, or the command line was wrong. Being over
quota is not an error \(em the number in the
.B % Used
column is the answer, not a failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
Your usage, one line:
.PP
.RS
.nf
quota_check
.fi
.RE
.PP
Which server is holding it all:
.PP
.RS
.nf
quota_check \-\-full
.fi
.RE
.PP
Someone else's usage, as an administrator:
.PP
.RS
.nf
quota_check \-u jdoe \-\-full
.fi
.RE
.PP
Percentage for a script or a status bar:
.PP
.RS
.nf
quota_check \-\-json | jq \-r '.percent'
.fi
.RE
.PP
The monthly over-quota mailing, checked before it goes out:
.PP
.RS
.nf
quota_check \-\-all \-\-email \-\-dry\-run
quota_check \-\-all \-\-email
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
Nothing outside bash and coreutils is required. TCP goes through bash's
.IR /dev/tcp ,
and so does SMTP, because the compute nodes have no local mail transfer
agent to hand a message to.
.PP
Under
.B \-\-all
the servers are queried in parallel for each user but the users are
walked one at a time, which keeps the daemons from seeing several hundred
concurrent connections.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sinteractive (1),
.BR getent (1),
.BR xfs_quota (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Jay Hesselberth. Rewritten in shell from the original Python
.BR quota_client.py .
